course: dictionary
lesson: 2772
title: Discuss: talking it through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To discuss something is to talk about it with others, sharing your ideas and opinions. You might discuss a story with a partner, or a maths problem with your group. Discussing means listening as well as talking. «You can choose your own clothes or haircut by discussing it with your parents, within family rules.» So you talk it through with your parents, and they listen to you too.
explain: Discuss has a second meaning, about writing. To discuss a topic in writing is to write about it and look at different sides, not just one. «People still discuss whether it is fair» means people keep talking and thinking about the question, because they have not all agreed yet.
explain: Look at the words around discuss to find its meaning. It is often followed by the thing you talk about, such as a problem, an idea or a question, and it is often used with words like with. «A case is a short story given to the teams to discuss, before or during the competition.» The teams talk about the story together, so discuss means talk about it with others.
fact: To discuss means to talk about something with others, sharing ideas and opinions.
fact: The verb forms are discuss, discusses, discussed and discussing.
fact: In school, you can discuss a story, a problem or a question in pairs or groups.
fact: A good discussion means listening to each other and giving reasons.
fact: Useful phrases: discuss with, discuss a problem, discuss ideas.
exercise: In maths you discuss how you solved a problem. What does discuss mean here? | Hide your answer from your group | Solve the problem alone and never say a word | *Talk together about how you solved it, sharing your ideas | Copy the answer from the board
exercise: «Women and children first» was an old rule for shipwrecks; people still discuss whether it is fair. What does discuss mean in this sentence? | People are writing a poem about ships | *People keep talking and thinking about whether it is fair | People have finished and all agree it is fair | People have forgotten the old rule
exercise: Which is a good way to discuss a story in class? | Read the story aloud and stop listening | Keep your ideas secret | Write your name on the story | *Share your ideas and listen to your partner
test: «You can choose your own clothes by discussing it with your parents, within family rules.» What does discussing mean here? | Buying clothes with your parents' money | *Talking it through with your parents and listening to them | Arguing until someone shouts | Choosing clothes without asking anyone
test: In writing, to discuss a topic means to do what? | Draw a picture of it | *Write about it, looking at different sides | Copy it from a book | Write only one side of the story
exam: Which sentence uses discuss to mean write about a topic from different sides? | The bus was late again this morning | *Today people still discuss how to judge the Reformation | The dog ran across the park | Ella sat quietly and ate her lunch
